From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the shell is asked for no local network permission

Every time the launcher opened, the desk asked to "access other devices
on your network" and "apps and services on this device". The launcher
draws a bookmark's tile from its site's /favicon.ico, and a bookmark on
the LAN or on localhost is a Local Network Access request from the
shell's document.

domicile:// has no IP address, so ChromeContentBrowserClient left it
kUnknown, which LNA reads as public: every fetch it made into the
network or the machine was a request for LOCAL_NETWORK or
LOOPBACK_NETWORK, prompted for, and never remembered for an origin that
is not http(s).

The shell is the desktop, not a site, so it is classed loopback, as
chrome-search:// and chrome-extension:// already are. Its fetches are
then never more private than itself, and nothing is asked. Pages in a
<webview> are their own documents and keep LNA as they were.
---
 chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
index b5502fdd70..8269c6c21f 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
@@ -2285,6 +2285,13 @@ ChromeContentBrowserClient::DetermineAddressSpaceFromURL(const GURL& url) {
     return network::mojom::IPAddressSpace::kLoopback;
   }
 #endif
+  // Domicile's engine fork. The shell is the desktop, not a site: left
+  // kUnknown it reads as public, and every bookmark's favicon on the LAN or
+  // on localhost asks for local network access. Its guests are their own
+  // documents and are not affected.
+  if (url.SchemeIs(domicile::kDomicileScheme)) {
+    return network::mojom::IPAddressSpace::kLoopback;
+  }
 
   return network::mojom::IPAddressSpace::kUnknown;
 }
